From 370a960cd5941cfc4ed0958a28c36f50bc8f2de0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TC Lowe <111537227+TCLowe1982@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:30:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(server): optional turn-complete notification for
 companion tools

Local companion tools (memory, analytics, archival) have no way to learn
that a conversation turn finished. Since client extensions were removed
the only option is polling chats.lastMessageAt on a timer, which is
laggy, infers turn boundaries from a timestamp, and races concurrent
writes. This replaces the poll with a push.

Adds services/turn-notify.ts, mirroring services/discord-webhook.ts:
a validated configured URL, safeFetch, fire-and-forget, errors logged
and never thrown to callers. Differences from that precedent are a 2s
timeout so a stalled consumer cannot hold a generation open,
maxRedirects 0, and debug-level logging because an absent companion
tool is an ordinary state rather than an engine fault.

Payload is identifiers only -- chatId, userMessageId,
assistantMessageId, characterId, and an ISO timestamp. Consumers read
content through the existing API. That keeps the contract free of
payload-size, PII, and serialization concerns, and means it need not
change when message shape does.

Call site is generate.routes.ts, beside the existing
chunkAndEmbedMessages call -- the point that already means "this turn is
done". It fires once per completed turn and covers regeneration
(addSwipe) and continuation (updateMessageContent) as well as new
messages, since all three branches converge on savedMsg before it.

Placed deliberately OUTSIDE the memoryRecallVectorizerAvailable check:
a consumer that does not use embeddings must not depend on an embedder
being configured.

Guarded on a saved assistant message. Reaching the call site does not
prove the turn produced one -- a model that spends its whole budget on
reasoning returns empty, the engine reports "empty response", and
lastSavedMsg stays null. Announcing that would hand consumers a user
message with no reply: half a turn recorded as a whole one.

No-op unless TURN_NOTIFY_URL is set. No new dependency, no schema
change, no behaviour change when unset.

Verified against a dev instance: delivery over loopback (safeFetch
refuses private ranges by default, so the policy needed proving),
payload shape, silent no-op when unset or malformed, call-site execution
on a real generation, and no emission on either failed or
empty-response turns.
